.SH "NAME"
pcre2_general_context_create \- create a general context
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\f(CR\&#include <pcre2.h>

pcre2_general_context *\fP\f(CBpcre2_general_context_create\fP\f(CR(
      void *(*\fP\f(CIprivate_malloc\fP\f(CR)(size_t\fP \f(CIsize\fP\f(CR, void *\fP\f(CImemory_data\fP\f(CR),
      void (*\fP\f(CIprivate_free\fP\f(CR)(void *\fP\f(CIptr\fP\f(CR, void *\fP\f(CImemory_data\fP\f(CR),
      void *\fP\f(CImemory_data\fP\f(CR);\fP
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function creates and initializes a general context. The arguments define
custom memory management functions and a data value that is passed to them when
they are called. The \f(CIprivate_malloc\fP() function is used to get memory for
the context. If either of the first two arguments is \f(CBNULL\fP, the system memory
management function is used. The result is \f(CBNULL\fP if no memory could be obtained.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.